"Leveling raises an Avowed's authority beyond what their affixed abilities hold."
"The System turns that unbound excess into talent rewards: skills, spells, foundation points."
"Each reward resets the excess, though never to zero."
"An Avowed may refuse rewards and keep leveling unrewarded."
"Before forcing an affixation the System tries everything else, bribes included."
"Forcing is horrible on the System's budget and seen as monstrous."
"Too much excess authority damages the original affixation, bringing agonizing death or worse."
"Rabbits have less unbound authority than other classes by design."
